z5n = z5k (z3x + THROW_SAFE + RISK_TTL 40) + CASH_READ (new switch, Cfg.CASH_READ; Baby.cashTick). z5k passed zd191 on
every gate but overruns (D 3, net +3, t +1.77; 6 overruns, all in araid arrows B). In its dumped replay
(~/diag26b/ov5k, seed 0) rat 12846 overran at r1896, r1898 and r1900. Its costliest segment from r1881 on was stage
6-7, cashTick plus report(), at 2,948 rising to 9,130. That started with the CASH_END recall at r1880, when about 30 rats
packed round one king. cashTick read every squeak of the last five rounds (readSqueaks(-1); the engine keeps them 5
rounds), kept those of the last three, and fully decoded each SQ_CASH. A crowd relays one site, so the same code arrives
about 90 times. With CASH_READ it reads rounds r-2, r-1 and r one at a time (readSqueaks costs 10) and skips a copy of
the current best's code. The same site wins: a copy cannot beat the best under cashFirst, and -1 is never an SQ_CASH
code. So only the bytecodes change, and only on turns that pass cashTick's opening gate (CASH_BANK's low-bank rescue
or CASH_END from r1880).

